# Canonical author identities.
#
# `git shortlog`, `git log --use-mailmap` and GitHub's contributor list read this
# file. It maps the addresses that appear in commits onto one identity per person
# without rewriting history — which for a public repository is the point: a
# rewrite changes every SHA, and the SHAs are cited in issues, in image tags
# (`:sha-<short>`), and in this repository's own commit footers.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> <address-as-committed>
Stéphane Richard <stephane.richard@scality.com> <stef.richard@gmail.com>
